      "card_ids": ["C10"],
      "claim": "Larotaxel, a taxane structurally very similar to the query (same C-13 side chain and taxane core), demonstrated the ability to cross the blood-brain barrier and is minimally recognized by P-glycoprotein, directly supporting meaningful CNS access for the query.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C08"],
      "claim": "Merck-3, a P-glycoprotein substrate, showed undetectable brain concentrations after i.v. dosing in mice, illustrating that efflux can severely limit CNS exposure; however, this non-taxane small molecule is less mechanistically transferable to the taxane query than the direct taxane evidence.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "moderate",
  "decision_summary": "Predicted pass: the closest taxane analogue (larotaxel) directly crosses the BBB and is not subject to P-gp efflux, and the query shares the taxane scaffold and C-13 side chain. Non-taxane efflux liabilities are acknowledged but are outweighed by the taxane-specific experimental evidence.",
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct cabazitaxel BBB/CSF data are provided; prediction relies on the close analogue larotaxel.",
    "Quantitative extent of CNS exposure (e.g., brain-to-plasma ratio) for the query is not directly established.",
    "Potential species differences and the impact of the query's methoxy substitutions on P-gp recognition are not fully resolved."
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [],
  "revision_action": "initial"
}

